{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JdUaM58SYQVz7vYWFmxkBe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# H1 Minimum-Useful CBM Checkpoint Prompt\n2\t\n3\tStatus: pending non-current-model review\n4\tDate: 2026-05-07\n5\tScope: pass-claim\n6\t\n7\t## Task\n8\t\n9\tReview whether H1 clears the minimum-useful CBM floor. Write findings into `CHECKPOINT.md` and leave the final decision in `DISPOSITION.md`.\n10\t\n11\tThe current dev-agent model must not fill in reviewer identity, confidence, or disposition.\n12\t\n13\t## Pass Criterion\n14\t\n15\tH1 minimum-useful CBM floor: one pinned external target has a real runtime Surface Mapper output, a real isolated Skeptic review over that output, a structurally carried challenge/no-challenge result, a validated handoff with contestation and coverage honesty, and no deterministic-baseline overclaim.\n16\t\n17\t## Explicit Non-Claims\n18\t\n19\t- Not Phase B.\n20\t- Not standard mode.\n21\t- Not repeatability.\n22\t- Not beta readiness.\n23\t- Not mature CBM.\n24\t- Not cross-platform parity.\n25\t- Not broad product maturity.\n26\t\n27\t## Artifacts To Inspect\n28\t\n29\t- `VISION.md`\n30\t- `RUNTIME-CONSTITUTION.md`\n31\t- `.planning/HORIZONS.md`\n32\t- `.planning/CURRENT-PLAN.md`\n33\t- `.planning/STATE.md`\n34\t- `.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/PLAN.md`\n35\t- `.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/VERIFICATION.md`\n36\t- `.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/SUMMARY.md`\n37\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-02-mcp-git-surface-mapper-h1s1/RESULT.md`\n38\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s2b-skeptic/RESULT.md`\n39\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s2c-disposition/RESULT.md`\n40\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/RESULT.md`\n41\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/HANDOFF.md`\n42\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/VERIFY.md`\n43\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/LINEAGE.md`\n44\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/INCLUDED-ARTIFACTS.md`\n45\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/surface-map.json`\n46\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/skeptic-review-surface-map.md`\n47\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/source-h1s2c-handoff.md`\n48\t- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/evidence-ledger.jsonl`\n49\t\n50\t## Questions\n51\t\n52\t1. Did H1.S1 use a real runtime Surface Mapper producer?\n53\t2. Did H1.S2b use a real isolated Skeptic producer?\n54\t3. Was the H1.S2b challenge grounded in citations?\n55\t4. Was the H1.S2c disposition structurally carried into the surface/handoff path?\n56\t5. Does the final handoff preserve coverage honesty and unknowns?\n57\t6. Does the final handoff distinguish runtime evidence from deterministic/dev-fixture evidence?\n58\t7. Are artifact lineage and ledger caveats clear enough to audit?\n59\t8. Is the H1 pass claim scoped correctly?\n60\t9. Should the disposition be `accept`, `accept_with_blockers`, `revise`, or `reject`?\n61\t\n62\t## Allowed Dispositions\n63\t\n64\t- `accept`\n65\t- `accept_with_blockers`\n66\t- `revise`\n67\t- `reject`\n68\t\n69\tOnly `accept` clears the current pass-claim gate unless the repo policy is explicitly changed by the user and logged.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6cbc7cf-fde2-43ca-881c-5166caea7a38","uuid":"b49b32a5-3b5d-40b5-8e59-c0ff36509f5a","timestamp":"2026-05-08T02:31:01.557Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/rookslog/Development/cbm/.planning/reviews/2026-05-07-h1-minimum-useful-checkpoint/PROMPT.md","content":"# H1 Minimum-Useful CBM Checkpoint Prompt\n\nStatus: pending non-current-model review\nDate: 2026-05-07\nScope: pass-claim\n\n## Task\n\nReview whether H1 clears the minimum-useful CBM floor. Write findings into `CHECKPOINT.md` and leave the final decision in `DISPOSITION.md`.\n\nThe current dev-agent model must not fill in reviewer identity, confidence, or disposition.\n\n## Pass Criterion\n\nH1 minimum-useful CBM floor: one pinned external target has a real runtime Surface Mapper output, a real isolated Skeptic review over that output, a structurally carried challenge/no-challenge result, a validated handoff with contestation and coverage honesty, and no deterministic-baseline overclaim.\n\n## Explicit Non-Claims\n\n- Not Phase B.\n- Not standard mode.\n- Not repeatability.\n- Not beta readiness.\n- Not mature CBM.\n- Not cross-platform parity.\n- Not broad product maturity.\n\n## Artifacts To Inspect\n\n- `VISION.md`\n- `RUNTIME-CONSTITUTION.md`\n- `.planning/HORIZONS.md`\n- `.planning/CURRENT-PLAN.md`\n- `.planning/STATE.md`\n- `.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/PLAN.md`\n- `.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/VERIFICATION.md`\n- `.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/SUMMARY.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-02-mcp-git-surface-mapper-h1s1/RESULT.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s2b-skeptic/RESULT.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s2c-disposition/RESULT.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/RESULT.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/HANDOFF.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/VERIFY.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/LINEAGE.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/INCLUDED-ARTIFACTS.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/surface-map.json`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/skeptic-review-surface-map.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/source-h1s2c-handoff.md`\n- `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/evidence-ledger.jsonl`\n\n## Questions\n\n1. Did H1.S1 use a real runtime Surface Mapper producer?\n2. Did H1.S2b use a real isolated Skeptic producer?\n3. Was the H1.S2b challenge grounded in citations?\n4. Was the H1.S2c disposition structurally carried into the surface/handoff path?\n5. Does the final handoff preserve coverage honesty and unknowns?\n6. Does the final handoff distinguish runtime evidence from deterministic/dev-fixture evidence?\n7. Are artifact lineage and ledger caveats clear enough to audit?\n8. Is the H1 pass claim scoped correctly?\n9. Should the disposition be `accept`, `accept_with_blockers`, `revise`, or `reject`?\n\n## Allowed Dispositions\n\n- `accept`\n- `accept_with_blockers`\n- `revise`\n- `reject`\n\nOnly `accept` clears the current pass-claim gate unless the repo policy is explicitly changed by the user and logged.\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}}}
