{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LMGYde4GPZGpgZQwWhevg7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 01 Summary\n2\t\n3\tStatus: partial; intervention track complete, H1.S3 packet prepared, checkpoint pending\n4\tLast updated: 2026-05-07\n5\t\n6\tThe recovery intervention track closed the accepted Tier 1 and Tier 5 R-OK items from the Opus cross-vendor audit.\n7\t\n8\tCompleted:\n9\t\n10\t- Codex CLI runtime producer isolation was verified through `cbm run` on two scratch repos.\n11\t- The Codex adapter now records timeout cause, partial output, logs, and output/log hashes.\n12\t- `run_id` validation blocks path traversal before `.research/<run_id>` paths are constructed.\n13\t- Runtime skill loading has a formal `cbm.skills` compatibility module.\n14\t- `cbm checkpoint` can generate native checkpoint packets for cross-model review.\n15\t- `cbm-loop-status` blocks orphaned review packets and pass-claim checkpoints from the current model family.\n16\t- Deterministic baseline/dev-fixture outputs are labeled in handoffs and card titles.\n17\t- Per-phase planning artifacts now exist under `.planning/phases/`.\n18\t- `.planning/HORIZONS.md` now translates `VISION.md` into autonomous `/goal` stages.\n19\t- H1.S1 real Surface Mapper evidence passed on pinned MCP `src/git`: `surface-mapper@1.2` produced a non-baseline schema-valid `surface-map.json` with source citations and honest coverage.\n20\t- H1.S2a evidence-bundle repair completed the accepted post-H1.S1 Opus review blockers before real Skeptic review.\n21\t- H1.S2b real isolated Skeptic evidence exists on pinned MCP `src/git`: `skeptic@1.2` reviewed the H1.S1 surface map and raised cited challenge `chl-10001`.\n22\t- H1.S2c challenge disposition exists: `auth-001` is `contested`, and `chl-10001` is `accepted_as_alternative`.\n23\t- H1.S3 packet is prepared at `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/`; the non-current-model checkpoint skeleton is prepared at `.planning/reviews/2026-05-07-h1-minimum-useful-checkpoint/`.\n24\t\n25\tNot yet complete:\n26\t\n27\t- The true minimum-useful-CBM floor still needs a non-current-model checkpoint disposition accepting the H1 pass claim.\n28\t- Phase B+ runtime-agent orchestration is still not implemented.\n29\t- The next runtime-producer track should prove repeatability on another small external target before broader maturity claims.\n30\t\n31\tPhase 01 is not closed until the non-current-model checkpoint disposition accepts.\n32\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6cbc7cf-fde2-43ca-881c-5166caea7a38","uuid":"02335d14-993b-4b23-8821-0f2a7003af89","timestamp":"2026-05-08T02:31:24.377Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/rookslog/Development/cbm/.planning/phases/01-first-runtime-producer-evidence/SUMMARY.md","content":"# Phase 01 Summary\n\nStatus: partial; intervention track complete, H1.S3 packet prepared, checkpoint pending\nLast updated: 2026-05-07\n\nThe recovery intervention track closed the accepted Tier 1 and Tier 5 R-OK items from the Opus cross-vendor audit.\n\nCompleted:\n\n- Codex CLI runtime producer isolation was verified through `cbm run` on two scratch repos.\n- The Codex adapter now records timeout cause, partial output, logs, and output/log hashes.\n- `run_id` validation blocks path traversal before `.research/<run_id>` paths are constructed.\n- Runtime skill loading has a formal `cbm.skills` compatibility module.\n- `cbm checkpoint` can generate native checkpoint packets for cross-model review.\n- `cbm-loop-status` blocks orphaned review packets and pass-claim checkpoints from the current model family.\n- Deterministic baseline/dev-fixture outputs are labeled in handoffs and card titles.\n- Per-phase planning artifacts now exist under `.planning/phases/`.\n- `.planning/HORIZONS.md` now translates `VISION.md` into autonomous `/goal` stages.\n- H1.S1 real Surface Mapper evidence passed on pinned MCP `src/git`: `surface-mapper@1.2` produced a non-baseline schema-valid `surface-map.json` with source citations and honest coverage.\n- H1.S2a evidence-bundle repair completed the accepted post-H1.S1 Opus review blockers before real Skeptic review.\n- H1.S2b real isolated Skeptic evidence exists on pinned MCP `src/git`: `skeptic@1.2` reviewed the H1.S1 surface map and raised cited challenge `chl-10001`.\n- H1.S2c challenge disposition exists: `auth-001` is `contested`, and `chl-10001` is `accepted_as_alternative`.\n- H1.S3 packet is prepared at `.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/`; the non-current-model checkpoint skeleton is prepared at `.planning/reviews/2026-05-07-h1-minimum-useful-checkpoint/`.\n\nNot yet complete:\n\n- The true minimum-useful-CBM floor still needs a non-current-model checkpoint disposition accepting the H1 pass claim.\n- Phase B+ runtime-agent orchestration is still not implemented.\n- The next runtime-producer track should prove repeatability on another small external target before broader maturity claims.\n\nPhase 01 is not closed until the non-current-model checkpoint disposition accepts.\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
