{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GikkwnRzqycfWrWty8zzy9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tschema_version: '1.2'\n3\tartifact_type: handoff\n4\trun_id: run-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff-1\n5\tproduced_at: '2026-05-07T14:30:00Z'\n6\tproduced_by: cbm-handoff@0.1\n7\tsource_sha: 4503e2d12b79\n8\tinputs:\n9\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/surface-map.json\n10\t  sha256: db936e0bf054eb3545490c5edab052264b795f3586c569281f539406a728f3aa\n11\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/skeptic-review-surface-map.md\n12\t  sha256: 0ec18b269a1cfb8cc8c1609995c78164d1b8318d9b3535da64fa2a66a7c7736d\n13\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/source-h1s2c-handoff.md\n14\t  sha256: e325edea2c38f7778923e9200e3c4d7bc77df30976a8820928efee0a4b273b3d\n15\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/evidence-ledger.jsonl\n16\t  sha256: 7bcf6543af80ec3f4f60303c4136788bd7506ca821607a048bca84ab5278cc34\n17\tstatus: validated\n18\tcoverage:\n19\t  scope:\n20\t    included_globs:\n21\t    - '**/*'\n22\t    excluded_globs:\n23\t    - .git/**\n24\t    - .research/**\n25\t    - .venv/**\n26\t    - node_modules/**\n27\t    - '**/__pycache__/**'\n28\t    - .pytest_cache/**\n29\t    - .DS_Store\n30\t  result:\n31\t    files_in_scope: 12\n32\t    files_examined_directly: 7\n33\t    files_inspected_via_extractor: 12\n34\t    files_unread_in_scope: 0\n35\t  limitations:\n36\t  - Baseline extractor coverage saw every in-scope file; the runtime Surface Mapper directly examined only the files needed for interpretive claims.\n37\t  - No CI workflow files were present in scope, so CI gating could not be mapped.\n38\tmode: lightweight\n39\tuser_goal: prepare H1 minimum-useful CBM handoff for MCP git server surfaces\n40\tgoal_class: understand_repo\n41\tresearch_only: true\n42\tgate_summary:\n43\t  schema_validation:\n44\t    passed: 6\n45\t    failed_artifacts: []\n46\t  citation_resolution:\n47\t    resolved: 28\n48\t    unresolved_count: 0\n49\t    unresolved_examples: []\n50\t  ledger_consistency:\n51\t    append_only_verified: true\n52\t    entry_count: 37\n53\t  staleness_check:\n54\t    fresh: 5\n55\t    stale_artifacts: []\n56\t  skeptic_review:\n57\t    artifacts_reviewed: 1\n58\t    challenges_logged: 1\n59\t    challenges_resolved: 1\n60\tcontestation_summary:\n61\t  claims_by_register:\n62\t    factual: 11\n63\t    inferential: 2\n64\t    interpretive: 2\n65\t  claims_by_status:\n66\t    active: 14\n67\t    challenged: 0\n68\t    contested: 1\n69\t    contradicted: 0\n70\t    superseded: 0\n71\t    retired: 0\n72\t  open_challenges: 0\n73\t  contested_claims:\n74\t  - claim_artifact: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/surface-map.json\n75\t    claim_id: auth-001\n76\t    challenge_count: 1\n77\t    summary: auth-001 preserves the shared-command-implementation reading and carries chl-10001 as an accepted alternative distributed-routing reading.\n78\t  contradicted_claims: []\n79\tartifacts:\n80\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/surface-map.json\n81\t  artifact_type: surface_map\n82\t  status: validated\n83\t  summary: Final H1 surface state after H1.S1 mapper output, H1.S2b Skeptic challenge, and H1.S2c disposition.\n84\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/skeptic-review-surface-map.md\n85\t  artifact_type: skeptic_review\n86\t  status: validated\n87\t  summary: Real isolated skeptic@1.2 review over the H1.S1 runtime Surface Mapper artifact.\n88\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/source-h1s2c-handoff.md\n89\t  artifact_type: handoff\n90\t  status: validated\n91\t  summary: Source H1.S2c handoff carrying open_challenges 0 and contested auth-001.\n92\t- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/evidence-ledger.jsonl\n93\t  artifact_type: evidence_ledger\n94\t  status: validated\n95\t  summary: Preserved ledger including challenge_resolved for chl-10001 and documented historical caveats.\n96\topen_questions_count: 1\n97\tcoverage_caveats:\n98\t- Runtime Surface Mapper direct examination covered 7 of 12 in-scope files; extractor coverage saw all 12 in-scope files.\n99\t- No CI workflow files were present in target scope, so CI gating remains unmapped.\n100\t- MCP runtime dispatch through the external library remains partially opaque even though the in-repo registry is clear.\n101\trecommended_next_action_kind: prepare_pass_claim_review\n102\trecommended_next_action: Run the non-current-model checkpoint review of the H1 pass claim; do not move to H2 or Phase B until accepted.\n103\t---\n104\t# H1 Minimum-Useful CBM Handoff\n105\t\n106\t## Target\n107\t\n108\t- Repository: `https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers`\n109\t- Subtree: `src/git`\n110\t- Pinned SHA: `4503e2d12b799448cd05f789dd40f9643a8d1a6c`\n111\t- Local verification checkout: `/var/tmp/cbm-h1-mcp-servers-4503e2d/src/git`\n112\t\n113\t## Evidence Chain\n114\t\n115\tFinal H1 surface state = H1.S1 runtime Surface Mapper artifact + H1.S2b runtime Skeptic review + H1.S2c mapper response/disposition.\n116\t\n117\t- H1.S1 produced a real `surface-mapper@1.2` `surface-map.json` through backend `codex-cli`.\n118\t- H1.S2b produced a real isolated `skeptic@1.2` review over the H1.S1 map through backend `codex-cli`.\n119\t- H1.S2c accepted `chl-10001` as an alternative reading and carried the result into `surface-map.json` and the source H1.S2c handoff.\n120\t\n121\tThis handoff is the reviewable H1.S3 packet. It is not itself a new runtime reading and does not claim that H1 is complete before checkpoint acceptance.\n122\t\n123\t## Producer Honesty\n124\t\n125\tRuntime-produced evidence:\n126\t\n127\t- `surface-mapper@1.2`: original H1.S1 map of the MCP git server.\n128\t- `skeptic@1.2`: isolated H1.S2b review that raised `chl-10001`.\n129\t- `surface-mapper@1.2`: H1.S2c mapper response accepting the challenge as an alternative.\n130\t\n131\tDeterministic or baseline artifacts in the packet remain deterministic support material only. They are not promoted as runtime-agent understanding, and no `cbm-baseline-*` or `dev-fixture-*` artifact is used as a substitute for the real Surface Mapper or Skeptic evidence.\n132\t\n133\t## Coverage\n134\t\n135\tThe final surface map reports 12 files in scope, 7 files examined directly, 12 files inspected via extractor, and 0 unread files in scope. The direct-examination count is limited to the files needed for interpretive claims; extractor coverage is not treated as direct reading.\n136\t\n137\tLimitations:\n138\t\n139\t- No CI workflow files were present, so CI gating could not be mapped.\n140\t- MCP runtime dispatch through the external library remains partially opaque even though in-repo registry surfaces are clear.\n141\t- This is one pinned external target only; repeatability on a second target is not claimed.\n142\t\n143\t## Contestation\n144\t\n145\t`auth-001` is contested. The original reading treats `src/mcp_server_git/__init__.py` as the shared command implementation because the console script and module runner route into the same callable. The accepted alternative, `chl-10001`, reads launch/routing authority as distributed across packaging metadata and the module shim.\n146\t\n147\tThe accepted alternative is grounded in:\n148\t\n149\t- `pyproject.toml:25-26@4503e2d12b79`\n150\t- `src/mcp_server_git/__main__.py:1-5@4503e2d12b79`\n151\t- `src/mcp_server_git/__init__.py:7-24@4503e2d12b79`\n152\t\n153\tCurrent contestation state:\n154\t\n155\t- `auth-001.claim_status = contested`\n156\t- `chl-10001.status = accepted_as_alternative`\n157\t- `open_challenges = 0`\n158\t- `claims_by_status.contested = 1`\n159\t\n160\t## Unknowns\n161\t\n162\tThe final surface map still records unknown edges. The live unknown summary is that no CI workflow files were present in scope and MCP runtime dispatch through the external library remains partially opaque. This packet does not imply full codebase understanding.\n163\t\n164\t## Boundary\n165\t\n166\tPrepared claim: H1 has a reviewable minimum-useful-CBM packet for one pinned external target.\n167\t\n168\tUnaccepted claims:\n169\t\n170\t- H1 is not complete until a non-current-model checkpoint disposition accepts the pass claim.\n171\t- Minimum-useful CBM is not complete until that checkpoint accepts.\n172\t- Phase B or later is not passed.\n173\t- Standard mode, repeatability, beta readiness, mature CBM, cross-platform parity, and broad product maturity are not claimed.\n174\t\n175\t## Recommended Next Action\n176\t\n177\tRun the non-current-model checkpoint review using `.planning/reviews/2026-05-07-h1-minimum-useful-checkpoint/PROMPT.md`. The current dev-agent must not fill in reviewer identity, confidence, or disposition.\n178\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6cbc7cf-fde2-43ca-881c-5166caea7a38","uuid":"7bf512f6-cdd4-4622-b376-2019d38f14d4","timestamp":"2026-05-08T02:31:34.827Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/rookslog/Development/cbm/.planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/HANDOFF.md","content":"---\nschema_version: '1.2'\nartifact_type: handoff\nrun_id: run-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff-1\nproduced_at: '2026-05-07T14:30:00Z'\nproduced_by: cbm-handoff@0.1\nsource_sha: 4503e2d12b79\ninputs:\n- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/surface-map.json\n  sha256: db936e0bf054eb3545490c5edab052264b795f3586c569281f539406a728f3aa\n- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/skeptic-review-surface-map.md\n  sha256: 0ec18b269a1cfb8cc8c1609995c78164d1b8318d9b3535da64fa2a66a7c7736d\n- path: .planning/benchmarks/2026-05-07-mcp-git-h1s3-minimum-useful-handoff/source-h1s2c-handoff.md\n  sha25